# Valgrind suppressions for the runner's tests (.github/scripts/zig-valgrind.sh). Only reports known
# to be benign belong here, each with a comment saying why; a report that is a bug is fixed instead.
# zig-valgrind.sh prints a suppression for every report (--gen-suppressions=all) to copy from.

# Zig's std.Io.Threaded wakes a futex whose word lived in the waiting thread's frame (a Future it
# awaited), after that thread saw the result and returned, so the address is below its stack
# pointer. FUTEX_WAKE never reads or writes the word: the kernel only hashes the address to find
# waiters, of which there are none left. Memcheck checks the syscall's pointer argument as if it
# were read. Seen from Io.Threaded.Future.start (a test starting a job's concurrent tasks).
{
   zig-std-io-threaded-futex-wake-after-the-waiter-returned
   Memcheck:Param
   futex(futex)
   fun:os.linux.x86_64.syscall3
   fun:os.linux.futex_3arg
   fun:Io.Threaded.Thread.futexWake
}
